// RestartSandboxOnLatest POST /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/restart-on-latest: Restart a sandbox on the latest base. Restarts the machine on the newest base image, on its disk as it is: a running sandbox's disk is saved and it is stopped first (as `stop` does, without its memory), then it boots cold on the latest base. Memory is lost, and so are running programs. A running sandbox is never patched underneath: this is how an outdated one (`base.outdated`) moves on. Answers once it is starting. A sandbox starting, stopping or being deleted is `conflict`; one another call moves after this restart has stopped it is `aborted`. A key needs `sandboxes:write`. Experimental: `not_supported` unless the deployment has turned image patching on (`KANTEL_IMAGE_PATCHING`).
